{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And I will distress Ariel.</b> Jerusalem." "<b>And she shall be a mourning(?) [תאניה].</b> Like ואנחנו הדייגים (Isaiah 19:8), and some say from the root of אנה (Genesis 37:36), that nothing of her place shall remain." "<b>And she shall be to Me like Ariel.</b> For the altar is there from the burnt offerings, or like Ariel, for they shall all be slaughtered."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:43.181598843Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}